<!--
  AbxrLib IL2CPP managed-code-stripping preservation.

  Unity's IL2CPP linker strips managed types it cannot see referenced from code.
  AbxrLib types that are only ever instantiated from serialized assets - the
  AppConfig ScriptableObject loaded via Resources.Load, and the MonoBehaviours on
  the keyboard / PIN pad / exit-poll prefabs - have no direct code reference, so on
  release device builds (Medium/High stripping) they get pruned. At runtime that
  shows up as "The referenced script ... is missing!", the config deserializes
  empty, and initialization fails with "App identification not set".

  Preserving the two shipped runtime assemblies keeps every AbxrLib type regardless
  of the consumer project's Managed Stripping Level. Editor and Tests assemblies are
  excluded on purpose - they are never included in player builds.

  Unity automatically detects link.xml files inside a package, so no setup or
  relocation is required by the consuming project.
-->
<linker>
  <assembly fullname="AbxrLib.Runtime" preserve="all" />
  <assembly fullname="AbxrLib.UiRoundedCorners" preserve="all" />
</linker>
